title the shelf with nowhere left to fold -- a bound with no edge to check at, and the sweep's first proof
prompt Open as SILENCE under the INNER LOOP Standing block -- roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, council rota row N mod 5, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first, READ SCOPE -- pick up the running thread and take the infrastructure lane.
think Reds-first picked the work. Of the five open rows, %291/%295/%301 are Keaton's or booked, %306 is Pond's and %311 is Sound's language custody, leaving %301 -- five booked folds, one of which glow/gen closed hours earlier. Sizing the remaining four before moving anything was the whole lap: counsel/date/20260728 at 311, active-designing/yonder at 296, tools/gen/chapter at 434 with 2,992 inbound hits, tools/fixtures at 662.
think The mechanism, plainly: the mark law names exactly two fold shapes -- a room found by WHEN folds to <room>/date/YYYYMMDD/, a room found by WHAT folds to <room>/<letter>/ -- and counsel/date/20260728 is already the output of the first. tools/d/dated_path_resolve.rish builds <room>/date/<day>/<basename> as a pure function of the basename at line 140, so a directory below the day breaks the function that lets a stale reference be resolved rather than rewritten. That room has nowhere to go, and tools/fixtures/room_bound_scan.sh was printing it as roster=advise beside three rooms that do -- a header whose own words gloss that line as "a room over the bound has a real fold ahead of it". The meter was booking work the law cannot perform.
think A day shelf now prints terminal_shelf= with its headroom to GitHub's 1,000-entry listing cap, and gates nothing. Twice on purpose: 256 sits deliberately BELOW the cliff, so gating a shelf at the cliff is the placement this file's own header argues against; and the hour fold that would answer it -- date/YYYYMMDD/HH/, equally pure since the hour is characters 10 and 11 of the basename -- is a change to a seated law rather than a meter's to make. Reporting is the honest act. The dead undated_over variable, assigned zero and lost to the pipeline's subshell, is live now by reading the sweep from a temp file.
think Second finding, and it stopped the lap before the first: tools/r/room_bound_witness.rish was ALREADY RED on metal at lap open. Its control asserts the enforced roster size so a room joining has to be written down, and glow/gen joined ENFORCE_ALL in the peer's 9b58744ef while the number stayed at 7. The assert did exactly its job and nobody turned it. The roster lives in the scan and its size lives in the witness, so a one-room change is a two-file edit -- single-stranded read the same morning says to check a part by trying to pull it out, and this one does not come out alone.
think The rota read row 1, Air/Saturn, law and boundary, sense of touch: the threshold plus TAME_CORE cardinal, single-stranded fixed, GAUGE_STYLE dual. N is git rev-list --count HEAD at 3616 and 3616 mod 5 is 1; the previous Silence lap read row 0, so a clean advance and no hand-advance. The threshold governed the lap in one sentence -- a claim of a boundary is tested by pressing on it, and if the hand passes through, the boundary was a wish and the lap writes that down. TAME_CORE's first reflex is bound everything, name the budget at construction and CHECK AT THE EDGE; a day shelf is the case where the budget is named and there is no edge to check at.
obs The control's pen was not a git repository, so the undated sweep -- added yesterday for %301, and the mechanism that found all five rooms -- had never fired in a test. Every line it prints went untested for its whole life, because git ls-files reads nothing outside a repository. Phase three builds a real one, plants both shapes side by side, and proves seven readings from both sides by removing the plants. I checked the control bites rather than assuming it: planting a regression in the scan flips three of the seven and the verdict refuses.
obs Two claims in the witness had gone false and are corrected in the same lap: its GREEN line said "all seven enforced rooms" and "tools by every flat entry" where the roster is eight and two rooms count that way. Its header also claims every enforced room is asserted by name, and the two counted by flat entry -- tools and glow/gen -- were the exception. That is the wrong pair to leave unnamed, since counting by every flat entry is the rule tools/ needed after reading zero for its whole life at 7.4x the bound.
obs NO LEDGER ROW IS BOOKED, and that is the derived-spine law working rather than a lapse. Local construction/REDS.md stops at %314 while reds_spine_derive_scan.sh --next reads 316 from the anointed remote, so upstream holds a %315 this tree has never seen; booking %316 here would hole the spine that reds_ledger_monotone_witness gates at 1..N. Both findings are cited by stamp until the trees converge. The scan read 315 at lap open and 316 an hour later, so fetch-before-book earned its keep inside one lap.
obs The checkout has DIVERGED and I did not cross it. git merge-base --is-ancestor HEAD xy/main says no: local carries bd547d0e2, 391c92a5e and 9b58744ef unpushed -- the peer's glow letter-room fold -- while xy/main carries 0bb2b605f that we lack, forked at d75f9fac60. A pull --rebase would rewrite a live peer's commit hashes in a shared checkout, which is %291 with a sharp edge, so nothing is pushed. My 7 -> 8 turn is correct on this branch and wrong on xy/main, where ENFORCE_ALL still reads tools alone; the arc comment says which branch owns the turn.
obs Peer named at the open per %291 and told twice before any file moved: grain-38, writing in glow/ and the construction/ pins. My commit is path-limited to three files. The pre-commit hook was read before committing rather than trusted -- it git-adds README.md, and the peer had README.md dirty, yet its rule-one trigger fires only on an ADDED or DELETED witness and it refuses rather than sweeping a dirty page, so a modify-only lap cannot pull the peer's work into my commit.
obs No clean roster reading, said plainly. A cold standing_equipment_run.sh opened at lap start has been alive forty minutes with zero output while the peer writes continuously, so it is bound to refuse under tree_moved. That is %295 and %291 territory rather than a new red. The scoped gates ran instead and are green.
obs Found and not taken, for the lane that owns filing law: .claude/rules/design-rooms.md and its Cursor twin both say counsel's last dated file is 20260805.000001, and counsel/date/20260826/20260826-181924_the-instrument-and-the-artifact.md was committed 20260826.184631 -- a room declared closed grew twenty-one days later. Measured rather than booked, since the 764-pieces figure beside it still reads true at 763 date notes plus one in yonder, and the pair is gate %7 territory.
